     ccuuddaa — Apple CUDA I/O Controller Driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee aaddbb
           ddeevviiccee ccuuddaa

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ccuuddaa driver provides support for the CUDA VIA (Versatile Interface
     Attachment) chip found in pre-Core99 Apple hardware, such as the Power
     Macintosh G3.

     The Apple CUDA controller is a multi-purpose ASIC that provides power
     control and an adb(4) interface.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
